## Context

Author request, 2026-10-29, corrected the same day. The first draft read
"weight loss, round 2" as another one-off trim of `skills/harness-doctor/`
(round 1: `3dc7ef05`). That was a misreading. The author wants a **routine
checkup**: on each visit the doctor offers to take the harness's vital signs,
so that a weight-watch discussion rests on measured trends, not impressions.

Second author note, same day: think KPIs, starting with time per ticket. The
monitoring already stores what a quick pulse check and basic follow-up need;
the checkup reads it, it adds no instrumentation.

Existing stores and readers to reuse, not duplicate:

- Time per ticket: `scripts/slow_tickets.py` defines solve time once (sum of
  the `duration:` lines gaze, verify-gate and merge post on the PR; else PR
  open-to-merge, an upper bound; else unknown).
- Cost per ticket: `scripts/trace-stats.py` (tokens, USD per session) joined
  to PRs by `scripts/trace-pr-join.py`.
- Review outcome: REROLL / ESCALATE verdicts (`trace-pr-join.py`, review notes).
- Main health: `idh/after-merge.log`, `idh/main-journal.jsonl`.
- Throughput and backlog: ticket `Created:` / `Closed:` headers, `/dashboard`.
- Size and timings: `scripts/skill_text_lint.py` (body length, long blocks),
  `scripts/gaze_wall_time.py`, `scripts/trace-wall-time.py`.

## Intent

Add a checkup to the visit menu of `skills/harness-doctor/SKILL.md`, offered
at the start of every visit, in two panels.

**KPIs (pulse)**, over the window since the previous visit:

- **Time per ticket**: median and p90 solve time, share recorded vs derived vs
  unknown, the slowest tickets named.
- **Cost per ticket**: median and total USD and tokens.
- **Throughput**: tickets closed, opened, net backlog change.
- **First-pass quality**: share of PRs merged without REROLL or ESCALATE;
  red after-merge runs on main.

**Vital signs (weight)**:

- **Length**: lines (and words or tokens) of every `skills/*/SKILL.md`, its
  references, the resident rules, and every script under `scripts/`.
- **Complexity**: a cheap structural proxy per script (functions, branches or
  cyclomatic complexity) and per skill (steps, probe rows, cross-references).
- **Main timings**: wall time of the expensive paths: gaze, the test gate,
  session start, from existing traces where they exist.

Each figure is shown beside the previous visit's (stored in the visit journal
entry), so the report reads as a delta: biggest gainers, totals, outliers. The
checkup measures and surfaces; whether to cut, and what, is the weight-watch
discussion with the author that follows, not part of the checkup.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The visit menu offers the checkup at every visit; one command produces it
- [ ] Report covers the KPIs (time and cost per ticket, throughput, first-pass quality) and length, complexity and main timings, each with the delta to the previous visit
- [ ] Every figure comes from an existing store; a KPI whose store is missing or unreadable is reported as a gap, never as zero
- [ ] Figures are recorded in the visit journal entry so the next visit can compare
- [ ] A first run on origin/main is attached to the PR as the baseline
- [ ] Cost stated in the menu row (seconds, no model usage) and a positive control fires
